.TH RESTARTWHY 1
.SH NAME
restartwhy \- find processes using deleted executable mappings
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B restartwhy
[--pid PID] [--format json]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Scans visible Linux process mappings for files marked deleted. Such mappings can
indicate processes that need a restart after a package or executable update.
This is evidence only: it does not restart processes or change service state.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --pid PID
Inspect one process instead of all visible processes.
.TP
.B --format json
Emit the versioned JSON report (the only supported format).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 means no deleted mappings were found; 1 means one or more were found; 2
invalid usage; 3 partial visibility; and 4 a runtime failure.
